  "notes": "Drawn from N168FE (767-300F, July 2026). The FedEx logo is a wordmark, drawn as titles. Freighters have no windows. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on N168FE: 'Express' runs x 0.247 to 0.325 under the 'Ex', 'The World On Time' 0.038 to 0.105 under the cockpit, the engine's 'FedEx' 0.28 to 0.53 of the nacelle; the wordmark's lowercase stands about 0.72 of its capitals. One photo, from a little ahead, so the big title's place was left as drawn. Re-traced 2026-11-20 on N168FE with tools/photo_trace.py: the aft purple's edge was 0.025 to 0.05 aft all the way up, meeting the crown behind the fin's root and leaving a strip of white crown under the fin (seen in a 3D view); it reaches the crown at the fin's root (0.829).",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximate standard (a few colors from memory). The FedEx livery came with the 1994 rebrand from Federal Express."
